{"at": "2026-11-20T18:29:14Z", "class": ["state", "platform"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-d371203106d1", "review:sha256-20b364949486", "owner:turn@2026-11-20T18:01:57.271Z#798c82d8ebd4"], "id": "3a79a07f57ebd0b8", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "c151660a-2c59-5f31-a015-fa23aea172ca", "text": "Scheduled tasks that wake one chat do not carry over a handover. When the owner ends a chat while an every-hour rule is running: make the last release, record a pause with the time and his words (the hours between chats then show as paused, neither missed nor done), disable that chat's tasks, and write into the procedure that the next chat creates its own and ends the pause.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-20T18:29:14Z", "class": ["career"], "evidence": ["gate:check exit 0", "owner:turn@2026-11-20T18:01:57.271Z#0681249819e2"], "id": "64a194bec23095b8", "kind": "note", "scope": "family:career", "session": "c151660a-2c59-5f31-a015-fa23aea172ca", "text": "Owner, 20 Nov 2026, on his job search: mostly hybrid and in-person roles, less remote. Keep remote postings but rank them lower, give search and research time to local employers first, and name local postings first when reporting what is new.", "trust": "owner-stated"}
